  "engine": {
    "id": "elektron-model-cycles",
    "name": "Elektron Model:Cycles",
    "description": "Elektron Model:Cycles FM groovebox: every parameter of its manual's MIDI appendix, as the controllers and NRPNs it prints, on the track and FX channels.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "type": "manual",
        "title": "Model:Cycles User Manual, OS 1.13",
        "notes": "MIDI appendix read by tools/profiles/elektron/read-elektron-midi.mjs from Model-Cycles-User-Manual_ENG_OS1.13_241030.pdf (sha256 2a6bdd8843d84743206ff980b63f38f6b67b5bb52ba6aa97afd28e6a33664f50), https://www.elektron.se/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/Model-Cycles-User-Manual_ENG_OS1.13_241030.pdf. Not yet checked against the instrument itself."
      }
    ],
    "testedWith": [],
    "authoringNotes": [
      "Generated by tools/profiles/elektron/make-profiles.mjs; edit the layout in tools/profiles/elektron/synths/, not this file.",
      "Every parameter is a row of the manual's MIDI appendix, with its printed name, sent on the CC it prints (a 14-bit pair where it prints an LSB), or its NRPN where it prints no CC. Nothing here has been sent to a real instrument yet.",
      "The appendix prints no ranges: each parameter takes what its controller carries, 0 - 127 (0 - 16383 for a pair). What a value shows, and the values of a setting chosen from a list, are in the parameter's chapter of the manual.",
      "The channel variable is a track's channel (track 1's by default): the parameters go to that track. Set it to the AUTO channel to edit whichever track is active.",
      "The fxChannel variable is 16 here: the manual prints no default for it; set it to the instrument's FX IN (SETTINGS > MIDI > CHANNELS) setting."
    ],
    "variables": {
      "channel": 1,
      "fxChannel": 16
    },
